title: The Recipient's View
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Open ''Import Invoices'' from ''More › Importers''.  The page is the
introduction you wrote, a source box, and one green button.

# ''Get the JSON in.''  Paste it, drop the file on the box, or use the file chooser.  The status line under the box says at once whether it is valid JSON -- and, if not, the line and column where it goes wrong.  ''Try it with the sample'' loads the sample that shipped in the pack, for a first run with nothing at stake.
# ''Stage invoices.''  Nothing is written yet.  The ''Results'' table counts what was produced; ''Staging'' lists every tiddler about to be written.  Expand a row to read its fields and text.
# ''Review.''  A title that already exists in the wiki appears under ''Conflicts'' with //skip// chosen; the recipient can pick //overwrite// or //rename// per row, or for all at once.  New titles default to //add//.
# ''Apply.''  The kept tiddlers are written and the staging area clears.  ''Imported this session'' lists them with links until the wiki is reloaded.

''Screenshot needed:'' the page after ''Stage invoices'' on the sample
-- the Results table and the three staged invoices, one expanded.

Everything else is fixed: the profile, the key/value flattening, the
collision default.  There is no dropdown to pick the wrong profile from
and no editor to break it in.  The recipient's working data -- the
pasted text, the results, the staged tiddlers -- lives under
`$:/temp/json-convert/invoice-importer/` and is never saved with the
wiki; only ''Apply'' writes ordinary tiddlers.
